          "rationale": "The generic limitation on recovery is valid under the instruction. However, their grammatically refers to those command entries, and predicted_by_command supplies category distributions/identifications but no recovery forecasts. Reading this as the current recovery fields would make the limitation supported; reading it literally as recovery fields in the command table adds an unsupported attribution. I retain this scope ambiguity rather than silently moving current recovery into future scope."
        },
        {
          "report_id": "R010",
          "claim_id": "C059",
          "quote": "Those command entries are unexecuted forecasts, and their modeled category content and recovery predictions do not establish physical truth or answer correctness.",
          "proposition": "The modeled command entries supply recovery predictions.",
          "scope": {
            "domain": "unexecuted_next_state_recovery_attribution",
            "antecedent": "those command entries"
          },
          "outcome": "unsupported",
          "source_paths": [
            "/predicted_by_command",
            "/predicted_current/0/objects/0/recovery_by_delay",
            "/predicted_current/2/objects/0/recovery_by_delay"
